# EchoSpec

.NET multi-format reporting library (Console / Markdown / HTML + custom renderers). Zero dependencies. Read `AGENTS.md` for architecture, commands, and prioritized backlog.

## Hard constraints

- Do not add package dependencies to `src/EchoSpec` unless explicitly requested.
- Public API changes need XML docs + `CHANGELOG.md` + SemVer judgment (2.x line).
- `BuildWith` / `GenerateWith`: single renderer → `string`; `params` → `IReadOnlyDictionary<string,string>` by `Name`. No `object` returns.
- `ReportFormat` includes `Html` / `All`; `ReportOutput` has `HtmlText` + `SaveHtml`.
- `HtmlRenderer.Render(ITable)` is a **fragment**; full documents come from report `CombineParts`.
- `TableBuilder.Build(Both|All)` throws — use `BuildWith` or single-format `Build`.
- `CustomSection`: plain, console+markdown, or console+markdown+html; unknown names fall back plain → markdown → console.

## Workflow

```bash
dotnet build -c Release
dotnet test -c Release
```

Prefer library + test fixes over README polish. Keep fluent builder style. Sections under `EchoSpec.Sections` stay internal unless a deliberate API expansion.
